+[tips-and-tricks-item-name]
+apm-fuel-chaining=Fuel chaining
+apm-fuel-leech=Burner inserters refuel from machines
+apm-ash-chaining=Ash in machine chains
+
+[tips-and-tricks-item-description]
+apm-fuel-chaining=An inserter between two burner machines also passes fuel along: when the first machine has at least 5 fuel and the next one less than 5, it moves fuel into the next machine's fuel slot.\nSo a row of [entity=apm_assembling_machine_0] only needs fuel at the start of the row.
+apm-fuel-leech=A [entity=burner-inserter] without fuel takes some from the fuel slot of the machine it takes from or puts into, even when it only carries other items. It only takes fuel it can burn and leaves at least one item in the slot.
+apm-ash-chaining=Burner machines produce [item=apm_generic_ash]. An inserter that moves items from one burner machine into the next one also moves the ash along, into the next machine's burnt-result slot, as soon as there is a batch of it (10% of the ash stack; checked about every 17 seconds). The inserter at the end of the chain puts it into a chest or onto a belt.\nSo one inserter at the end of a chain clears the ash of the whole chain.
